⛬  Draw.TextFixed is the answer. It places text at fixed screen 
   positions (TopRight, BottomLeft, Center, TopLeft, BottomRight) 
   that never move when you scroll. The Y-position (price level) can 
   be matched to the zone/line price. This is exactly what NT8 uses 
   for built-in indicators.

   The limitation: Draw.TextFixed only has 5 fixed positions and 
   doesn't let you specify a Y price. But it does stay anchored. For 
   labels that need to sit at a price level, I need a different 
   approach — I'll use Draw.TextFixed for labels with a custom 
   y-pixel offset calculated from the price level.

   Actually, the real solution is simpler: Use Draw.Text with the 
